WEBVTT

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.910
Neku?

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.870
Are you all right?

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.870
I'm sure of it.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.830
He murdered me.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.210
Neku?

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.000
Are you not feeling well?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.090
How can you look at me like that?

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.510
Did you remember something?

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.810
You need to work with your
partner to win the game.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.640
If you want to save that girl Shiki...

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.100
You get the idea.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.690
Damn it!

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:50.450
Until the Reapers' Game is over,
I'll protect you,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.280
and I want you to help me.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.740
What are you after?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.790
I want to properly guide Shibuya.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:02.920
You said that before.
Give me more details.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.300
Do you remember who controls Shibuya?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.170
The Composer?

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.630
Is you trying to meet the Composer?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.020
There's a high-energy
signature down this alley.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.060
And the Composer's there?

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.600
I think they might be.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.400
You'll help me, won't you?

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.120
"Sir, I bear a rhyme excelling

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.870
in mystic force and magic spelling.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:45.130
Celestial sprites elucidate..."

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.870
That's Minamimoto.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.130
Quiet. He'll spot us.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.750
Everything's ready.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.720
Wh-What's going on?

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.480
It appears that my phone
was reacting to this thing.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.270
What incredible energy.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.570
A Taboo Noise Refinery.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.120
Looks unfinished, though.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.700
This is starting to smell fishy.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.210
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.510
Turf

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.220
Another day passed?

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.430
Hello, Mr. Hanekoma?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.810
It's me.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:13.020
There's no mission again today.
We should be able to stop by.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.310
Two more days.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:13.020
Will we really be able to
clear the game at this rate?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.150
He killed me.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.820
I could never trust him.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.830
But I have to win this game,
no matter what.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.700
This is for Shiki.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.080
I can't afford to lose.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.500
What's wrong?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.630
Nothing.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:38.130
Hey, I'm going to see Mr. Hanekoma.
You'll come with me, won't you?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.840
Look.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.590
I'm getting hits all over Shibuya.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.640
There's no mission either.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.140
Come on.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.350
Fine.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.220
Miyashita Park Underpass

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.480
It's closed.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.610
I don't see a way around.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:58.740
Our only option is to open the wall.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.360
Open it? How would we...

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.070
Hey, that graffiti on the wall!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.490
It's Noise!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.220
Maybe the wall will open if we beat them.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.090
I won't make it?

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.670
Found you!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.180
Yo, Phones!

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.390
What?!

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.310
Neku?!

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.310
Stand up.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.030
I'm gonna wipe the floor with you!

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.360
Beat, you...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.280
Why are you doing this?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.200
'Cause I'm a Reaper!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.160
I don't want to fight you.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.710
What? You wimping out? What a letdown!

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.420
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.960
You've got to play by the rules.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.760
We can only attack Players
directly on day seven.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.430
And even then, only the
Game Master gets to!

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.470
I'm runnin' a special op for Kitaniji!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.350
For Mr. Kitaniji?! Why would he pick <i>you</i>?!

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:56.060
Would you get lost?
You're in my way, <i>old timer</i>!

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.650
Come on, your phone's ringing.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.150
Who is it?!

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.860
Hello?!

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.740
Oh, Ms. Konishi?!

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.450
Oh, yes. Right.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.240
I'll get right on it.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.950
Taboo Noise again?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.080
Yup.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.920
What a drag.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.500
Well, let's go.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.460
Hey, you!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.590
Next time you mouth off to me,
you're dead! Got that?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.840
Just try it.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.100
Come on, rookie. Help us out here.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.890
Hey, what the hell?!

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.350
Let go, damn it!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:37.440
Bye. See you around.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.860
Just you wait!

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.320
What is he after?

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.700
A pendant?

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.660
What is it?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.580
This is...

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.500
...Rhyme's pendant.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:04.550
He might have his reasons
for turning Reaper.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:11.180
Neku, the wall is open, at least.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.180
Let's hurry to Mr. Hanekoma's.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.930
Cat Street

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.730
Mr. Hanekoma.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.520
Oh, there you are.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.190
Here. I need this fixed.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.230
You sure did a number on it.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.690
Hey.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.200
Not coming in?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:32.280
I'll... wait out here.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.290
Oh, Nekky!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.250
There you are again.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.000
You're from...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.300
Where's Josh-Josh?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.720
He's in that café, Wildkat.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:52.390
You'd better stick with your partner.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.720
It looks like we're the only Players left.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:09:00.270
I wanted some alone time.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.190
I've been doing some thinking

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.530
about how your partner
got taken as your entry fee.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:12.910
Yeah?

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:17.490
That just shows how much
you care about her, yeah?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.700
Totally!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:23.750
I'd be happy being Sota's entry fee
if it meant he got to come back.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.760
And I'd play this game as
many times as it takes for Nao!

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:31.510
This whole time,

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.760
I've been wondering if Shiki blames me.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.810
No way!

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:39.270
It's not like you did anything wrong.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.100
Yeah! So, it's totally fine.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.730
As long as everyone makes it back
in the end, it's no big deal!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.190
Everyone? It's not that easy to...

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.990
No. You're right.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.200
Thanks.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.330
Don't beat yourself up about it!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.250
Yeah.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.000
You've gotta enjoy yourself.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.040
Yeah. You said it, Nao.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.040
Everyone, huh?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:11.510
All kinds of people with all
kinds of issues live in Shibuya.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:15.090
'Course, you're all I need, Nao.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:15.090
Till next time.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.760
Don't break it again.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.260
Does he...

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:19.680
...have his reasons too?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.680
I think that will depend on Neku.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.430
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:31.860
"Under Construction"
"We appreciate your cooperation
and apologize for theinconvenience"

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.780
Is that store gone?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.410
It was a cool place.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.620
You know a lot about Shibuya, huh?

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:40.240
I grew up around here.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.620
I walked around Shibuya after school.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.960
With friends?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.170
I didn't know anyone I liked talking with.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.590
I thought so.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.550
Those headphones are proof that you
don't want to get involved, right?

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:00.510
Where'd this come from?

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.390
You know, Neku,

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:07.350
you're closed off just
like the Underground.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:11.150
You have walls between you and others.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.950
The Underground is divided into areas.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:19.240
The Shibuya Underground,
the Shinjuku Underground...

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:23.950
They each have their own rules.
You can't move between them.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.710
Remind you of anyone?

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:31.670
I thought that my own
world was all I needed.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.920
CAT's graffiti...

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:39.640
"Enjoy every moment with all you've got"?

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.810
It shocked me.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:46.810
Do what you want, when you want,
as much as you want.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.190
I wanted to do that,
but I'd given up on it.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.980
I just had to act on
the values I believe in.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.280
I felt like CAT told me that.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.240
That's true.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.290
You can't understand
other people's values.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:07.210
You don't need to bother
communicating with everyone.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.420
I wonder about that.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:15.710
She-- Shiki...

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.550
...had a fight with her friend
and never talked it out.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.680
But when she heard how
her friend really felt,

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.100
she looked happy.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.770
I didn't notice back then,

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.570
but Shiki's smile was so happy.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.820
You've really changed, Neku.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.120
It's fascinating.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.370
Miyashita

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.370
Miyashita

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.790
New CAT graffiti!

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:56.260
Shibuya really is full of
CAT's work, isn't it?

00:12:56.260 --> 00:13:00.510
I'm amazed he can find
the time to run a café.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:03.510
CAT runs a café? Is it in Shibuya?

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.520
You've been there a few times now.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.480
He's Mr. Hanekoma.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.850
Who is?

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.350
CAT.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.860
Huh?

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:15.020
CAT is Mr. Hanekoma.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.450
Mr. Hanekoma is CAT?!

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.780
Are you serious?!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:22.950
It's true.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.030
Hey! Wait, hang on! Calm down!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.370
For real?!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.880
Mr. Hanekoma is CAT.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.550
I always thought there was
something different about him.

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.300
Hang on, I've been talking with CAT?!

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.180
Whoa! That's crazy!

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:46.600
Is it <i>that </i>exciting?

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:50.100
Oh no! Did I say anything rude to him?!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.390
No, scratch that.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.860
I tried to tell CAT about CAT.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.070
I...

00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:00.320
I'm such an idiot!

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:04.660
Don't let him know I told you.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.120
S-Sure.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:10.830
OK!

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:20.760
Is today going to end without a mission?

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:25.260
It's a high-energy signature!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.760
It's over toward...

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.520
I hope we manage to find it this time.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.020
Hey, hang on.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:36.560
You're planning to take on
the Composer, right?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.570
Something like that.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:41.570
In that case, I'm out.

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:44.610
I've got to win this game.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.240
I don't want extra risks.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.200
All right,

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.500
but I'd at least like
to check out the place.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.830
I'll be satisfied with taking a look.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.880
You can have your way after that.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.300
You better mean it.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:03.550
I won't get you any more involved.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:06.300
If I can go two more
days without trouble...

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:11.350
Let's go check it out. But that's all.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:12.640
Thank you.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:17.900
It's just the other side of the
Shibuya Station Underpass.

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:28.030
Talk about creepy.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.290
Hey, are you sure this is the right way?

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:32.410
I am.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.210
It's in here.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.170
We checked it out.
You'd better be satisfied.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.470
I know. I'll keep my promise.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:47.090
Either way, it appears there's a wall.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.390
Sure it's not just dark?

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.770
It's a bit different from
the others we've seen.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:58.230
I'll have to figure out how to remove it.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.400
Shibuya Station Underpass

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.530
Does something feel off to you?

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:18.460
It's Noise.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:20.130
What are those?

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:23.130
Black Noise, like the ones
outside Tokyu Hands.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.140
Looks like normal attacks
really don't work.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.640
Let's attack together.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:37.850
On it.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:55.990
Neku!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:08.970
Are you all right?

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.180
Yeah.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:17.810
I don't think we have
what it takes to win now.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.230
If we can't win, we've gotta run!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.690
No.

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:25.230
I don't think we can.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:27.360
Not good.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.950
Damn it! Is this it?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.660
I've got no choice.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.950
I was reluctant to do this, but...

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.890
What? Whoa.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:59.180
You can do that?!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.770
It really wears me out, so I'd rather not.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:03.650
I saw that.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:05.730
You're--

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:10.570
Sorry, this time I'm here
for pretty boy there.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:13.110
I knew it.

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.910
You're not dead.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.660
Huh? What do you--?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.700
It was that move you used.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:23.580
I've never seen power like
that in the Underground.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.590
Players can't use anything like it.

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:29.800
Playing while alive is against the rules.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.260
That said,

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:36.220
those Taboo Noise were a problem,
so I'll let it slide this time.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:42.680
But next time we meet,
I'll erase you in no time flat.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.020
Uzuki will, anyway.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.480
See you.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:53.030
The Noise are gone now, so let's go, Neku.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:54.240
Wait.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.160
You're... alive?

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:01.620
Was that Reaper telling the truth?

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.660
The cat's out of the bag.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:08.460
That's right. I'm playing the
game while I'm still alive.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.880
What the hell?

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.970
There are always loopholes.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:18.850
Although, since I entered illegally,
I don't have a Player pin.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.270
But don't worry.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:24.980
I can make Partner Pacts,
so I'm the same as any other Player.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:26.980
Like hell...

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:28.940
Like hell you are!

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.730
You're alive, but your just like us?!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.940
That's a load of crap!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.950
You <i>chose </i>to come to the Underground.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:40.990
But the rest of us didn't!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:44.540
We never asked to end up here!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.330
We're not...

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.420
...playing this game for the fun of it!

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:53.960
You're playing to come back to life.
Isn't it a good deal?

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:57.630
It's your fault! <i>You </i>killed me!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:03.180
And I'm saying, so what if I did?

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.180
Huh?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:10.610
If I were the one who killed you,
Neku, what would you do to me?

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:15.280
Would you kill me, like when
you tried to kill Shiki?

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.990
How do you...?

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:19.110
I'm sure you weren't there.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.200
I told you.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:26.960
I've been watching you for a long time.

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.370
Since when?!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.920
Why?! What for?!

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.460
Why me?!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:35.960
That's because...

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.930
...this is your salvation too.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.350
Taboo Noise Refineries?

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:48.640
A living Player is a big enough
problem on its own.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:52.900
It looked like the Refineries
hadn't been used yet.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:58.450
The Taboo Noise must be
coming from somewhere else.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.950
You hear that another
Reaper got taken out?

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.570
In Dogenzaka, right?

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.240
They showed up by Tokyu Hands before that.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:07.910
Nowhere's safe lately.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.920
Minamimoto is making them attack Reapers?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.500
I think it's possible.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:17.670
Mr. Minamimoto was drawing
Taboo Noise Refineries,

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:22.180
so it's easy to suspect
he's behind everything.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:24.510
Insufficient evidence.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:27.680
A bunch of our people
have gotten taken out!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.190
It was...

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:35.940
...my first time being attacked by
Noise since I became a Reaper.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:42.110
I hate to admit it,

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:44.990
but I doubt I could have
survived on my own.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:51.000
I'll make a report to
Mr. Kitaniji tomorrow.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:53.750
You are to continue your investigation.

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:55.840
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:00.920
Is that going to be soon enough?

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:13.310
This is a zetta fun time!

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:15.980
I'll keep inverse calculating the world!

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:18.070
Two days till my solution!

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:21.820
Look forward to it, hectopascals!

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.920
Joshua

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:01.630
Next time, "Joshua."
